egory":"Nightlife","historical_business_count":5},{"category":"Cajun/Creole","historical_business_count":4},{"category":"Restaurants","historical_business_count":8}],"history":[{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Cajun/Creole, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":5},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"stqWlKEgXweNQSsxOsHjVA","review_id":"TCAR8BMgudyVL2WmgYdRFw","date":"2012-11-13T03:15:10","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9493873715400696,"text_excerpt":"I heard so many people rave about this place being one of the best po boy places in new orleans. I must say this place is really good, a bit pricey, but worth it in a way. The po boys were as big as they can get, and I loved how they had their thinly sliced onions there. Perfect to add into the po boys too. I had the typical cat fish poboy. But I also tried the roastbeef and spicy sausage poboy. Just delish! Only con here...LONG WAIT Overall great place for poboys!"},{"business_id":"stqWlKEgXweNQSsxOsHjVA","review_id":"iYw2tzkzeoaUkV61D1VSNg","date":"2013-06-02T17:12:57","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9402834177017212,"text_excerpt":"New Orleans offers up some of the best Po-boys anywhere. Combinations that I would never think of. Take Mahony's, huge selection of sandwiches. Everything from the standard Shrimp Po-boy to Zapp's Potato Chips Po-boy. My favorite is a \"French Fries. Roast Beef & Gravy, Cheddar Cheese\" Po-boy!! LOL! Greatness. Located on Magazine Street, West of the French Quarters, the restaurant is inside an old house with fairly large amounts of dining space inside and a few tables outside. Unfortunately for us, we came on graduation weekend. The place was packed front to back and inside-out. As we arrived there was about a 15-20 minute wait in line to order and then another 45 minutes to one hour wait ..."},{"business_id":"stqWlKEgXweNQSsxOsHjVA","review_id":"6hWPaBkEXm2TnBYlISVTZw","date":"2013-01-01T17:13:06","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9393340945243835,"text_excerpt":"This place was pretty legit - we were recommended to go here by some locals and I don't have a comparison since we didn't eat any other po boys while in NOLA. I got a full 12\" shrimp, fried green tomatoes and remoulade po boy. Also tried some friend oysters of our dining companions. The po boys come on french bread - which is really good, but also HUGE and kinda takes away from all the topping on it - well IMHO - just a little too much bread. Taste wise it was all really good - price wise the 12\" shrimp was only $5 or so more than the 6\" although the smaller one is more than enough - I shared with my bf - he also got the fried oyster po boy. We tried some onion strings and some cole slaw ..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"stqWlKEgXweNQSsxOsHjVA","photo_id":"agx6aRUi2nP4pB2mEqQXFw","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/agx6aRUi2nP4pB2mEqQXFw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8658791184425354},{"business_id":"stqWlKEgXweNQSsxOsHjVA","photo_id":"89QQZ9yl4mE458SOZoN7xQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/89QQZ9yl4mE458SOZoN7xQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8651670813560486},{"business_id":"stqWlKEgXweNQSsxOsHjVA","photo_id":"DDzZ9DEJaeoT5qvuhiLqBw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/DDzZ9DEJaeoT5qvuhiLqBw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8050906658172607},{"business_id":"stqWlKEgXweNQSsxOsHjVA","photo_id":"h_yv91MH8QIrlNe2dWRrHw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/h_yv91MH8QIrlNe2dWRrHw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7919642925262451},{"business_id":"stqWlKEgXweNQSsxOsHjVA","photo_id":"a2NM9O1OnVQG3GKO4yJrHQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/a2NM9O1OnVQG3GKO4yJrHQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7732158899307251}]},"notebook_case":null}
